<title>PHILIPPINES: Meralco B falls 3.23 pct.</title>
<headline>Meralco B falls 3.23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manila Electric Corp (Meralco) class B shares dropped four pesos, or 3.23 percent, to 120 pesos in early trade on Friday on foreign selling, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Meralco is a play on the economy, any weakness on the economy, perceived or otherwise, affects this stock,&quot; said Mayenne Katimbang, research head at Magnum International.  </p>
<p>&quot;Two foreign houses have been selling down Meralco B all the way from 140 pesos,&quot; said Jose Ricardo Garcia, executive vice-president at Diversified Securities.</p>
<p>Meralco A shares, reserved for local investors, were lower by 50 centavos at 81 pesos.</p>
<p>Some 1.26 million Meralco B shares and 8,500 A shares changed hands in early session.</p>
